  "gameChessHow": "Play White against the phone. Tap a piece, then the square to move it to: the possible moves light up. All rules apply: castling, en passant and promotion. Checkmate wins. The higher the level, the further ahead the phone thinks.",
  "gameCheckers": "Checkers",
  "gameCheckersHow": "Italian checkers: you have the light pieces, at the bottom. Men move forward diagonally and capture by jumping an enemy piece; capturing is compulsory and you must take the route that captures the most. A man cannot capture a king. Reaching the far row makes a king. You win by blocking or capturing everything.",
